  "content": {
    "id": "p13-q13-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "13",
    "prompt": "Simplify\n$$\\frac{1}{1+\\log_a(bc)}+\\frac{1}{1+\\log_b(ca)}+\\frac{1}{1+\\log_c(ab)}.$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$1$.\n\nUse change of base to give all three fractions the denominator $\\log(abc)$.",
      "worked": "Let $S$ denote the given sum. Using the product law and change of base,\n$$\\begin{align*}S&=\\frac{1}{\\log_a(abc)}+\\frac{1}{\\log_b(abc)}+\\frac{1}{\\log_c(abc)}\\\\S&=\\frac{\\log a}{\\log(abc)}+\\frac{\\log b}{\\log(abc)}+\\frac{\\log c}{\\log(abc)}\\\\S&=\\frac{\\log a+\\log b+\\log c}{\\log(abc)}\\\\S&=\\frac{\\log(abc)}{\\log(abc)}\\\\S&=1.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 55
  },
